From: OpenWrt MT6990 repair <mt6990@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: usb: r8152: make the TX aggregation buffer size a module parameter

agg_buf_sz (16 KiB) sizes each of the four TX aggregation buffers and also
bounds the TSO size and the TX queue length. On a SoftBank Air 6 (MT6990,
xhci-mtk) with an RTL8156B adapter, TCP TX reached about 1.4 Gbit/s with
16 KiB and about 2.35 Gbit/s (2.5G line rate) with 64 KiB. Raising the
number of TX buffers instead did not improve it. Which effect of the
larger buffers (fewer USB transfers, larger TSO, deeper queue) made the
difference was not isolated.

Expose agg_buf_sz as a read-only module parameter. The default stays
16384, so behaviour is unchanged unless the parameter is set. Parsed
values outside 16384-65536 are replaced by the default with a warning.
The parameter applies to every device the driver binds.

--- a/drivers/net/usb/r8152.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/r8152.c
@@ -1271,7 +1271,15 @@ enum tx_csum_stat {
  * The RTL chips use a 64 element hash table based on the Ethernet CRC.
  */
 static const int multicast_filter_limit = 32;
-static unsigned int agg_buf_sz = 16384;
+#define RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_DEFAULT	16384
+#define RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_MAX		65536
+
+/* Size of each TX aggregation buffer. It also bounds the TSO size and the TX
+ * queue length.
+ */
+static unsigned int agg_buf_sz = RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_DEFAULT;
+module_param(agg_buf_sz, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(agg_buf_sz, "TX aggregation buffer size in bytes (16384-65536, default 16384)");
 
 #define RTL_LIMITED_TSO_SIZE	(size_to_mtu(agg_buf_sz) - tp->tx_desc.size)
 
@@ -10212,6 +10220,14 @@ static int __init rtl8152_driver_init(vo
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	if (agg_buf_sz < RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_DEFAULT ||
+	    agg_buf_sz > RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_MAX) {
+		pr_warn("r8152: agg_buf_sz %u out of range %u-%u, using %u\n",
+			agg_buf_sz, RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_DEFAULT,
+			RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_MAX, RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_DEFAULT);
+		agg_buf_sz = RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ_DEFAULT;
+	}
+
 	ret = usb_register_device_driver(&rtl8152_cfgselector_driver, THIS_MODULE);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
